Subject: windows.web: HttpClient, HttpMethod, request and response messages and content, over winhttp

HttpBaseProtocolFilter now sends requests through winhttp instead of failing them as if offline: with its redirect,
decompression and cookie settings, the request's headers and body (read through IHttpContent), and the whole
response read before its operation completes (HttpCompletionOption.ResponseContentRead). Response headers are split
between the response's and its content's collections; after redirects the request's RequestUri is where the
response came from. Cancelling an operation closes its request.

New classes: HttpClient (with a filter, default request headers, Get/Post/Put/Delete/Send and GetString/GetBuffer/
GetInputStream), HttpMethod (statics and factory), HttpRequestMessage, HttpResponseMessage, HttpStringContent,
HttpBufferContent, HttpStreamContent and HttpMediaTypeWithQualityHeaderValue. Header collections hold name/value
pairs (IMap and IIterable of HSTRING pairs, Append, TryAppendWithoutValidation); the typed value collections parse
values into the header (ParseAdd, TryParseAdd, and Accept's IVector of media types). Other typed header views,
IHttpClient2/3 and transport information are not implemented.

